                                    <h1>Google Merchant Center + Shopping Feed Optimisation for D2C 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Google Merchant Center + product feed quality determines Google Shopping + Performance Max performance more than any other lever. Poor feed = poor performance regardless of bid strategy. Well-optimised feed can lift Shopping ROAS 40-80%. Here is the complete 2026-2027 optimisation playbook.</p>
                                    <h2>The 8 Feed Fields That Matter Most</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>title:</strong> Primary ranking factor. 70-150 characters. Product name + brand + key attributes + category.<br>2. <strong>description:</strong> Detailed 500-1500 characters. Keywords + benefits + specifications.<br>3. <strong>image_link:</strong> High-quality primary product image. 800x800+ recommended.<br>4. <strong>additional_image_link:</strong> 6-10 supporting images.<br>5. <strong>google_product_category:</strong> Google taxonomy category assignment.<br>6. <strong>product_type:</strong> Your custom category hierarchy.<br>7. <strong>gtin:</strong> Global Trade Item Number for brand + manufactured products.<br>8. <strong>brand:</strong> Product brand name.<br>Missing / poor quality any of these 8 damages Shopping performance materially.</p>
                                    <h2>Title Optimisation Framework</h2>
                                    <p>Title structure for e-commerce:<br><strong>Brand + Product Name + Key Attribute + Variant + Category:</strong><br>Example (bad): 'Cotton Shirt'.<br>Example (good): 'Snitch Slim Fit Blue Cotton Casual Shirt for Men — Size Medium'.<br><strong>Include:</strong> brand + specific product name + size + colour + material + gender / age + category.<br><strong>Avoid:</strong> promotional text + generic descriptions + capitalisation abuse + special characters.<br>Title optimisation typically lifts Shopping impressions + CTR 30-60%.</p>
                                    <h2>Feed Disapproval Common Causes + Fixes</h2>
                                    <p>Common disapproval reasons + fixes:<br><strong>Landing page mismatch:</strong> Product price + availability + image must match Merchant Center feed.<br><strong>Missing GTIN:</strong> For branded products, provide GTIN or use identifier_exists=false for custom / handmade.<br><strong>Restricted / prohibited products:</strong> Health claims + adult products + regulated items require compliance.<br><strong>Missing images:</strong> Every product needs primary image.<br><strong>Poor image quality:</strong> White background + high resolution + product-only images preferred.<br><strong>Content policy violations:</strong> Misleading + prohibited claims disapproval.<br><strong>Missing structured data on site:</strong> Product schema on PDPs required.<br>Regular disapproval monitoring + fixes essential — disapproved products = zero Shopping performance.</p>
                                    <h2>Custom Labels + Bidding Strategy</h2>
                                    <p>Custom labels (custom_label_0 to custom_label_4) enable advanced bidding:<br><strong>custom_label_0:</strong> Margin tier (high / medium / low) — higher bids on high-margin.<br><strong>custom_label_1:</strong> Sale status (regular / clearance / seasonal).<br><strong>custom_label_2:</strong> Best sellers / top performers vs long-tail.<br><strong>custom_label_3:</strong> Seasonal + category-specific tags.<br><strong>custom_label_4:</strong> Testing + experimental flag.<br>Custom labels enable Shopping campaigns segmented by profitability + performance vs generic all-product campaigns.</p>
                                    <h2>Feed Refresh Cadence</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Real-time API:</strong> Ideal for high-volume + fast-moving inventory.<br><strong>Daily scheduled refresh:</strong> Standard for most D2C brands via feed URL.<br><strong>Weekly refresh minimum:</strong> Below this, stale feed damages performance.<br><strong>Content API integration:</strong> Shopify + WooCommerce + Magento + Salesforce Commerce Cloud have official integrations.<br><strong>Third-party feed management:</strong> Feedonomics + Channable + DataFeedWatch for complex catalog management.<br>Feed freshness directly correlates with Shopping performance — stale feed = stale performance.</p>
                                    <h2>Performance Max Integration</h2>
                                    <p>Performance Max requires optimised feed as foundation:<br><strong>Feed quality drives PMax targeting</strong> — poor feed limits Machine Learning capability.<br><strong>Custom labels enable PMax segmentation</strong> — separate campaigns by margin + performance tiers.<br><strong>Asset groups + feed alignment</strong> — creative + feed + audience signals combined.<br><strong>Enhanced conversions</strong> — first-party data + feed data combined for better attribution + optimisation.<br>Feed optimisation is 60-70% of PMax performance. Bid + creative strategy secondary.</p>

